file:**\n\n1. **ApiError.kt**: Add `SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS` to ErrorCode enum after `SHIPMENT_ALREADY_EXISTS`. This code signals that a shipment's current status does not allow the requested operation.\n\n2. **ShipmentController.kt**: Add a new POST endpoint `@PostMapping(\"/{shipmentId}/confirm\")` that:\n   - Receives a shipment ID as a path variable\n   - Calls repository.findById(shipmentId) \n   - Throws ResourceNotFoundException if not found (404)\n   - If status is CONFIRMED, returns the shipment unchanged (idempotent)\n   - If status is CREATED, updates shipment to CONFIRMED, saves via repository.save()\n   - If status is CANCELLED, throws ConflictException with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS (409)\n   - Returns ResponseEntity.ok() with the (possibly unchanged) shipment\n\n3. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt**: Add four tests:\n   - `confirms a CREATED shipment moves it to CONFIRMED` - creates S-1, confirms it, asserts status=CONFIRMED\n   - `confirm is idempotent for CONFIRMED shipment` - creates, confirms, confirms again, asserts still CONFIRMED and no error\n   - `rejecting confirm of CANCELLED shipment` - manually saves a CANCELLED shipment, attempts confirm, asserts 409 with SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\n   - `rejecting confirm of non-existent shipment` - attempts confirm on missing ID, asserts 404 with SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\n\n**Alternative rejected:**\n- Could have added a separate service layer (ShipmentService) to isolate business logic, but the existing OrderController puts all logic in the controller. Consistency with existing patterns is more important than architectural purity for this scope.\n- Could have used a method parameter object instead of inline logic, but the four-case pattern is simple enough inline.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n| Case | Input | Read | Write | HTTP Status | Response |\n|------|-------|------|-------|-------------|----------|\n| Confirm CREATED | shipmentId | findById → Shipment(CREATED) | save Shipment(CONFIRMED) | 200 | Shipment(CONFIRMED) |\n| Retry CONFIRMED | shipmentId | findById → Shipment(CONFIRMED) | none | 200 | Shipment(CONFIRMED) |\n| Reject CANCELLED | shipmentId | findById → Shipment(CANCELLED) | none | 409 | {\"error\":{\"code\":\"SHIPMENT_INVALID_STATUS\",\"message\":\"...\"}} |\n| Reject missing | shipmentId | findById → null | none | 404 | {\"error\":{\"code\":\"SHIPMENT_NOT_FOUND\",\"message\":\"...\"}} |\n\n**Test strategy:**\n- Test 1 (CREATED→CONFIRMED): Verifies the state transition and persistence\n- Test 2 (idempotency): Verifies retry safety and no error on re-confirmation\n- Test 3 (reject CANCELLED): Verifies the 409 conflict response with correct error code\n- Test 4 (missing shipment): Verifies the 404 not-found response with correct error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1060,"cache_read_input_tokens":18787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1060},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"59772bfe-bd25-4456-bf1a-de70f2a877c5","uuid":"e6799b55-cf1d-4a7c-80db-5ebd12059533","timestamp":"2026-09-09T18:00:20.165Z","request_id":"req_011CetJSrPdKvDGXGcXCUoxZ"}
